{"title":"Career Roadmap: Conservation Architect","role":"Conservation Architect","summary":"A Conservation Architect specializes in the documentation, assessment, conservation, restoration, adaptive reuse, and sensitive development of historic buildings, monuments, precincts, and cultural landscapes.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Arch"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["ID","Level","Discipline","Degree","Specialization","Target Career"],"rows":[[{"text":"620"},{"text":"UG"},{"text":"Architecture, Planning & Design"},{"text":"B.Arch (Bachelor of Architecture)"},{"text":"Heritage Conservation Architecture"},{"text":"Conservation Architect"}]]}]},{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Conservation Architect specializes in the documentation, assessment, conservation, restoration, adaptive reuse, and sensitive development of historic buildings, monuments, precincts, and cultural landscapes."},{"type":"p","text":"The role combines:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Architecture"},{"text":"History"},{"text":"Heritage studies"},{"text":"Building conservation"},{"text":"Materials science"},{"text":"Structural understanding"},{"text":"Documentation"},{"text":"Archaeology"},{"text":"Urban planning"},{"text":"Community engagement"},{"text":"Digital technologies"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A modern Conservation Architect must balance:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Heritage Significance","Authenticity","Structural Safety","Function","Sustainability"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Typical projects include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Historic houses"},{"text":"Temples and religious buildings"},{"text":"Forts"},{"text":"Palaces"},{"text":"Colonial buildings"},{"text":"Historic public buildings"},{"text":"Heritage streets"},{"text":"Urban heritage precincts"},{"text":"Industrial heritage"},{"text":"Adaptive-reuse projects"}]}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons",